```

### The CSS-var cascade gotcha (the bug I lost 20 minutes on)

CSS custom properties cascade DOWN the DOM tree, not sideways. So:
- `:root` is `<html>` — sets the dark vars
- `body.light { --bg-0: ... }` sets `--bg-0` for `<body>` and all its descendants

But `getComputedStyle(documentElement).getPropertyValue('--bg-0')` reads
the value from `<html>`, which still has the original `:root` value.
`getComputedStyle(document.body).getPropertyValue('--bg-0')` returns
the overridden value (because the var cascades down from body).

If your canvas-rendered visualization reads from
`getComputedStyle(document.documentElement)`, it gets the WRONG theme
in light mode — the body shows light gray, the canvas keeps drawing
white text on transparent (invisible).

**Fix**: scope the override to `html.light` instead of `body.light`.
Then `getComputedStyle(documentElement)` returns the light values.

### Canvas code that respects the theme

The canvas can't read CSS via `style.color`. You have to query the
computed variables each frame (cheap) and use them:

```js
function draw() {
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  const cs = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
  const edgeColor = cs.getPropertyValue('--asm-edge').trim() || 'rgba(56,232,255,0.18)';
  const labelColor = cs.getPropertyValue('--asm-label').trim() || '#e6edf3';
  const particleColor = cs.getPropertyValue('--asm-particle').trim() || 'rgba(124,92,255,0.18)';
  // ... use edgeColor, labelColor, particleColor
}
```

Reading CSS vars in a 60fps render loop is fine — `getComputedStyle`
is cached for the frame. Don't try to be clever and read once on
theme change; the recompute is negligible.

## Responsive: 4 breakpoints, mobile sidebar collapse

The setup:
- Desktop: fixed 250px sidebar, main wrapper has `margin-left: 250px`
- ≤ 1200px: tighter stat cards, smaller hero/donut
- ≤ 992px: sidebar 200px, hides section labels
- ≤ 768px: **sidebar collapses to 64px icon-only**, expands to 250px on tap
- ≤ 576px: 1-column, header buttons hide, search wraps

```css
/* 1200px — compact */
@media (max-width: 1200px) {
  .stat-card .value { font-size: 24px; }
  .severity-donut { width: 150px; height: 150px; }
}

/* 992px — narrower sidebar */
@media (max-width: 992px) {
  .sidebar-nav-wrapper { width: 200px; }
  .main-wrapper { margin-left: 200px; }
  .nav-section { display: none; }   /* section labels like "TOOLS" */
}

/* 768px — collapsed icon-only sidebar */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .sidebar-nav-wrapper {
    width: 64px;
    transition: width 0.25s ease;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }
  .sidebar-nav-wrapper.expanded {
    width: 250px;
    box-shadow: 4px 0 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
